            <ArticleTitle>[Mites allergy in children from Tula region].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Characteristics of allergy to mites in children living in Tula region have been revealed. It was shown that mites from Pyroglyphidae (Dermatophagoides pteronyssinus, Dermatophagoides farinae), Cheyletidae and Glycyphagidae (G. destructor, G. domesticus) families play important role in development of atopic allergy in children from this region. Efficacy of plant-origin acaricide &quot;Milbiol&quot; as part of prophylactic measures was evaluated. Its use in children with mild and intermediate asthma led to decrease of number of wheezing episodes, improvement of respiratory function, lessening of clinical signs of allergic rhinitis, decrease or discontinuation of usage of vasoconstrictive preparations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
